# Dark Tides — The Legend of the Five Rings Game Master's Kit Adventure

**Version:** 0.4
**Source:** Legend of the Five Rings Roleplaying Game — Game Master's Kit (the Dark Tides adventure booklet; product L5R05)
**Publisher:** Fantasy Flight Games

> GM-facing narrative for the Game Master's Kit adventure. The full scene-by-scene procedure —
> objectives, checks, clues, and resolutions — lives in `l5r5e-0.4-gm-kit-dark-tides.arc`; the mechanical
> content (the Tortoise Minor Clan, the Kasuga family, the Kasuga Smuggler School, and the NPC
> statblocks) in `l5r5e-0.4-gm-kit-mechanics.ttrpg`. This adventure uses the players' own characters
> (at least one Emerald Magistrate is assumed), so there are no pregens. It is the first appearance of
> the mahō-tsukai **Kitsu Sokori**, who returns as the antagonist of *Mask of the Oni*.

---

## Adventure Background

*Dark Tides* is a sandbox investigation adventure set in **Slow Tide Harbor**, the Tortoise Clan's obscure smuggling port. The PCs are sent to find **Otomo Hiroshige** — the wastrel, opium-addicted son of the influential Imperial noble Otomo Saneda, who fled to Slow Tide Harbor under the alias "Doji Hiroshige" and vanished from an alley near the Golden Dream opium den over two weeks ago. Briefed indirectly by the Crane courtier **Doji Hiroka**, the PCs travel to the port to investigate — and uncover a conspiracy to kidnap opium-addicted samurai and sell them to a mahō-tsukai for blood sacrifices. Hiroshige is only the most prominent of several vanished addicts (the Tortoise samurai Kasuga Toru and Kasuga Michiko, the rōnin Fubato, and the murdered Crab Yasuki Suzaku among them).

---

## The Setting: Slow Tide Harbor

Slow Tide Harbor (Taimana Choryu) is a thriving but obscure port of some 3,000 souls on a peninsula in a swampy lagoon off the Bay of the Golden Sun, northwest of Otosan Uchi. It is the **Tortoise Clan's** major holding and primary smuggling nexus — walls-less, lawless, and morally ambiguous, where gaijin goods are sold openly, opium is widely tolerated, and samurai are often indistinguishable from peasants. It sprawls into the Governor's Neighborhood, the Merchant District (the "smugglers' district"), the Dockside, and the seedy **Wallow** (its opium dens and flophouses, where the samurai have been disappearing). It is governed, barely, by the opium-indulging **Kasuga Mugatsu** and policed, reluctantly, by the shrewd magistrate **Kasuga Mikoto**. The theme throughout is composure — resisting the urge to cut down those whose crimes and squalor offend a samurai's sensibilities.

---

## The Conspiracy: Kitsu Sokori

The true villain is **Kitsu Sokori**, a mahō-tsukai conducting blood sacrifices to boost her supernatural power — the daughter of a Lion Kitsu lord, fallen to blood magic. She works through her agent **Gaku**, a large, formidable rōnin mahō apprentice with a distinctive neck tattoo who coordinates the kidnappings, ships the prisoners to Sokori, and lodges at Suitengu's Rest. The local operation runs through one of **three interchangeable culprits** — the GM chooses which is the true local villain:

- **Kasuga Yumiko**, an ambitious Tortoise smuggler funneling victims to Sokori until the time is ripe to swoop in, destroy the cult, and reap political rewards;
- **Boss Yaguro**, a declining crime lord of the Green Rest opium den, selling drug-addicted samurai to Sokori via Gaku to shore up his shrinking territory; or
- **Azif the Smooth**, a bold gaijin captain of the *Obedient Slave* from al-Bhagvar, smuggling people for profit on Sokori's behalf.

Around them turn the port's other crime lords (**Boss Hana** "the Flower" and **Boss Kizo**), officials, and informants. Sokori herself appears only at a distance during the climax, and is intended as a **recurring nemesis** — the GM should ensure she survives to trouble the PCs again.

---

## Act One: Investigation

A sandbox. From the **Inn of Many Paths** (run by **Chiyu**, where Hiroshige stayed four months), the PCs follow threads through the criminal underworld: the frightened Crane artist **Kakita Amano** (who publicly accused Boss Kizo and went into hiding), the world-weary Scorpion junshin **Bayushi Naizu**, the traumatized rōnin **Hade** (who witnessed Hiroshige's kidnapping and was struck by Gaku's mahō, leaving his stable Defiled terrain), the nervous moneylender **Doro**, the opium dens (managed by **Master Aoi** and **Master Awa**), and the burakumin village (whose forensic knowledge of Yasuki Suzaku's body reveals the captivity). The clues converge: every victim was an opium addict, all were last seen with a large tattooed rōnin (Gaku), and physical evidence (raw opium, mahō traces) points to an isolated **warehouse** on the outskirts.

---

## Act Two: The Warehouse

The PCs raid the warehouse — three barred doors, ruffian guards, and a prisoner holding area with bloodied iron manacles (one set scratched with "Hiroshige," another marking Suzaku's failed escape). The crates identify the villain (gaijin goods and Blue Flame for Azif; high-quality opium for Yaguro; goods from across the Sea of Amaterasu for Yumiko), and false shipping documents name the vessel that will carry the prisoners out — the *Obedient Slave*, the *Floating Destiny*, or the *Jealous Zephyr*. The prisoners were shipped out the previous night; a fight and a street chase follow, and an interrogated ruffian can point the PCs to the docks.

---

## Act Three: Battle at the Docks

A climactic nighttime battle as the villain's ship prepares to cast off with the prisoners in the hold. **Gaku** is aboard and fights to the death — he may use mahō or set the ship ablaze — while the chosen villain is either on the docks or aboard. Provoking Gaku (a TN 3 Command check) makes him shout his master's name: **Kitsu Sokori**. The PCs must board, defeat Gaku, and free the chained prisoners, perhaps from a burning ship. At dawn, once the last enemies fall:

At dawn the PCs spot a robed figure on a distant fishing boat in the lagoon — **Kitsu Sokori**, staring back with a cold chill of malevolent attention before she escapes, leaving the PCs a powerful new enemy.

---

## Conclusion

Interrogations confirm the kidnapped samurai were meant for Sokori's blood sacrifices. The outcome ripples through the Tortoise Clan (embarrassment at best, a purge or Imperial penalty at worst), reshapes Slow Tide Harbor's criminal balance, and — above all — establishes **Kitsu Sokori** as a recurring nemesis who may pull strings from the shadows in adventures to come, including *Mask of the Oni*.

---

## The Cast at a Glance

- **Kitsu Sokori** — the mahō-tsukai mastermind; a fallen Lion Kitsu (statblock in mechanics; returns in *Mask of the Oni*). **Gaku** — her tattooed rōnin mahō-apprentice agent.
- **The three interchangeable villains:** **Kasuga Yumiko** (Tortoise smuggler), **Boss Yaguro** (Green Rest crime lord), **Azif the Smooth** (gaijin captain). Other crime lords: **Boss Hana**, **Boss Kizo**.
- **Officials:** **Kasuga Mugatsu** (governor), **Kasuga Mikoto** (magistrate). **Informants & witnesses:** Chiyu, Kakita Amano, Bayushi Naizu, Hade, Master Aoi, Master Awa, Doro, Kasuga Nagato (harbormaster), Ojo (priest).
- **Victims:** **Otomo Hiroshige** (the primary target), Kasuga Toru, Kasuga Michiko, Fubato, Yasuki Suzaku. **Patron:** Doji Hiroka (for Otomo Saneda). (Full statblocks in the mechanics file; scene detail in the .arc.)
